: operating cash flow of $2.8 billion less capital spending of $265 million (computed from two filed figures). That is 22% of revenue. In FY2020 it was $1.4 billion.","cites":["MSI.ocf.2025","MSI.capex.2025","MSI.revenue.2025","MSI.ocf.2020","MSI.capex.2020"]},{"topic":"sbc","text":"Stock-based compensation was $293 million in FY2025, 2.5% of revenue, against 1.7% in FY2020.","cites":["MSI.sbc.2025","MSI.revenue.2025","MSI.sbc.2020","MSI.revenue.2020"]},{"topic":"returns","text":"In FY2025 the company paid $1.2 billion to repurchase its own shares and $728 million in dividends: $1.9 billion together (computed from two filed figures).","cites":["MSI.buybacks.2025","MSI.dividends.2025"]},{"topic":"quarter","text":"In the three months ended 2026-10-03 revenue was $3.4 billion, up 12.2% from $3 billion in the three months ended 2025-09-27.","cites":["MSI.d.revenue.2026-07-05.2026-10-03","MSI.d.revenue.2025-06-29.2025-09-27"]},{"topic":"ttm","text":"Over the four quarters to 2026-10-03 revenue added up to $12.6 billion (computed from five filed figures), operating income to $3.1 billion and net income to $2.1 billion.","cites":["MSI.d.revenue.2025-01-01.2025-12-31","MSI.d.revenue.2025-01-01.2025-09-27","MSI.d.revenue.2026-01-01.2026-04-04","MSI.d.revenue.2026-04-05.2026-07-04","MSI.d.revenue.2026-07-05.2026-10-03","MSI.d.opinc.2025-01-01.2025-12-31","MSI.d.opinc.2025-01-01.2025-09-27","MSI.d.opinc.2026-01-01.2026-04-04","MSI.d.opinc.2026-04-05.2026-07-04","MSI.d.opinc.2026-07-05.2026-10-03","MSI.d.netinc.2025-01-01.2025-12-31","MSI.d.netinc.2025-01-01.2025-09-27","MSI.d.netinc.2026-01-01.2026-04-04","MSI.d.netinc.2026-04-05.2026-07-04","MSI.d.netinc.2026-07-05.2026-10-03"]},{"topic":"ttm","text":"Free cash flow over the same four quarters was $2.5 billion: operating cash flow of $2.8 billion less capital spending of $304 million (computed from ten filed figures).","cites":["MSI.d.ocf.2025-01-01.2025-12-31","MSI.d.ocf.2025-01-01.2025-09-27","MSI.d.ocf.2026-01-01.2026-04-04","MSI.d.ocf.2026-01-01.2026-07-04","MSI.d.ocf.2026-01-01.2026-10-03","MSI.d.capex.2025-01-01.2025-12-31","MSI.d.capex.2025-01-01.2025-09-27","MSI.d.capex.2026-01-01.2026-04-04","MSI.d.capex.2026-01-01.2026-07-04","MSI.d.capex.2026-01-01.2026-10-03"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"The proxy statement filed 2026-04-02 gives the principal executive officer’s total pay for FY2025 as $34.5 million in its summary compensation table, and the “compensation actually paid” - the SEC’s measure, which revalues share awards over the year - as -$34.9 million.","cites":["MSI.pay.peoTotal.2025","MSI.pay.peoPaid.2025"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"For the other named executive officers the same table gives an average of $6.8 million in total and -$11 million actually paid.","cites":["MSI.pay.neoTotal.2025","MSI.pay.neoPaid.2025"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"The table puts the value of $100 held in the company’s shares over the years it covers at $239.54 at the end of FY2025, and $241.63 for the peer group the company chose.","cites":["MSI.pay.tsr.2025","MSI.pay.peerTsr.2025"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Remaining performance obligations - revenue under contract that was not yet recognised - were $9.6 billion at the end of FY2025, against $9.4 billion a year earlier. That is 82.2% of FY2025 revenue (computed from two filed figures).","cites":["MSI.rpo.2025","MSI.rpo.2024","MSI.revenue.2025"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Deferred revenue was $2.3 billion at the end of FY2025 (tagged ContractWithCustomerLiabilityCurrent), against $2.1 billion a year earlier.","cites":["MSI.deferred.2025","MSI.deferred.2024"]},{"topic":"people","text":"The latest annual report gives the workforce as 23,000 in its own words. FY2025 revenue works out to about $508,000 for each (computed from one filed figure and the number in that sentence).","cites":["MSI.q.employees","MSI.revenue.2025"]},{"topic":"debt","text":"At the end of FY2025 the balance sheet carried $1.2 billion in cash and cash equivalents, and $9.2 billion o